            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dora"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent Recipe, here are my modifications:\r\n- used Veg Ground Round instead of text veg protein\r\n- added a little white wine and only 2 cups of water, not 4\r\n- 2 cans of kidney beans used\r\n- 2 cloves of garlic only. I put everything in a crockpot (sauteed garlic, onions &amp; celery first) and left it on low all day until supper. Delish!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used ground turkey instead of vegetable protein, and used crushed tomatoes instead of stewed tomatoes. Only used 2 cups of water and had to add some corn starch to thicken it. Only used two cans of chilli beans instead of 4. It was very good.",
            "datePublished": "2021-02-12T20:02:35.003Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Monica"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow! This is good! I made some changes though: took the advice of some other reviewers and added a cup less water. I also used kidney beans as I couldn't find chili beans. I added a little white wine as someone else suggested. I added a bit more chili powder and a little cumin. I used turbinado sugar instead of brown sugar. I used petite diced tomatoes instead of stewed. Thanks for the recipe. I have faith in my ability to cook with TVP now. :)",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-12T16:38:17.790Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mer in the Kitchen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe was a great jumping off point for chili to feed a hungry potluck croud. I omited the celery (seeing as I didn't have any on hand). Due to another review, I cut down on the water by one cup. Then, when I doubled the recipe - I didn't have enough chili beans, so I substituted some kidney beans (drained) instead. I wanted my chili meaty, so I substituted about a pound and a half of browned ground beef for the second cup of TVP. The result was delicious. I am sure that it would be equally tasty made accoring to the recipe - but I would hold off on part of the water, and see how thick you want it.",
            "datePublished": "2006-11-28T19:40:11.140Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nasa999"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was my first time using TVP. It was great! This is a slightly sweet chili recipe, not very spicy at all. I used a can of black beans instead of one of the cans of chili beans, because that's what I had. I added cumin because I like that in chili. I also added a half a can of tomato paste because I had it left over and thought this would be a good way to get rid of it. I was very happy with this recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2015-01-11T15:22:31.917Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "VERONICAUJ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I halved the recipe, adding about a teaspoon of minced garlic, substituting one can of kidney beans for a can of chili beans, and adding about a cup of TVP, dry. My roommates and family absolutely loved it! I think it's my favorite chili.",
            "datePublished": "2005-03-09T20:02:22.560Z"
          },
